  "answer_core": "You should not lock in 15% equity, a CTO title, or a board seat this week. Those are permanent commitments you can only make once you know whether the partnership actually strengthens the company rather than concentrating risk in one person.\n\nTreat Friday as a direct, structured conversation about a staged path. Make clear that there is a real route to meaningful upside and leadership for him, but only after evidence. Define a short, explicit window to test whether he can deliver the key platform work, whether that work proves revenue‑relevant, whether team continuity improves, whether knowledge transfer happens, and whether his behavior fits the governance you need. Also be clear about what success in that window would unlock.\n\nThis avoids both a premature commitment and a vague delay. Give him a credible, time‑bounded path tied to demonstrated impact rather than hypothetical valuation math.",
